|money drop = 200¢ - 790¢
}}

==Enemy==
Aku Doge has very high DPS, even more than [[Gabriel]], but still has short range and single-target attacks like the original [[Doge]]. His only ability is a [[Shield]] that regenerates with 50% HP after each damage-based knockback he takes; this Shield starts with the same amount of health as Aku Doge himself, so it effectively gives him 2.5x as much HP if you don't use any [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]]. Additionally, he has the range of a typical meatshield (110), so he can block your single-target Shield Piercers such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs]] and [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]] from hitting more dangerous [[:Category:Enemies with Shields|Shielded enemies]] like [[Fallen Bear]] and [[Wicked Face]].

==Strategy==
Use strong attackers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] or [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] if there is only one Aku Doge. If there are multiple, use strong [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] like [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] or [[Ancient Egg: N006 (Special Cat)|Fallen Bear Cat]]. Repeated attacks from these units will quickly tear through his [[Shield]] and health, meaning he isn't that much of a threat. Another great way to dispose of single Aku Doges is to use [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]], as it can break the Shield with its initial attack and kill off the Doge with the wave. The Aku Doge's attack will also destroy Jellycat, easing stalling in stages like [[Seahorses Caught]] as you don't have to worry about hitting the base early.

Interestingly, [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] at level 20+89 can take three hits from a 600% Aku Doge (his strength magnification in [[Uncanny Legends]], early [[Zero Legends]], and many other late-game stages), whereas [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] at level 50 can only take two.

